BnNYwxHOqfoqgSqe/12/rzs9+7CtH9VsWE3kFNVo7wVG+Yq\n/hJMsvdvlR6Jxz8Ugz5PWMNb7MKG/1ki+XOKnGqEQ/7ocP+wuxFifawaaGSo\n1GjLMc+15Eu6JJzecfFQxxc51khciANv5XkoY4dQGpQKttjuUDpYTphNB7Nd\nsCOTrqq7jXwJ4fqgOk0N1Sc9DA+nFm4xjOFGeHufWS78J4HVgz52MR6Lb95C\nBjRuWRlMVQsiOkM9ame8auSGBkylYeSWySZEvA==\n",
    "teacher_markdown": "## Student Directions: Wiring Your Custom App Data to the Display\r\n\r\nYour task is to populate and display data for three items in your **custom app** using the schema you designed in the previous level. This exercise uses **parallel arrays** and **manual indexing**.\r\n\r\n1.  **Update HTML and CSS:** Upload the picture of your schema and work with AI to update the `index.html` and `style.css` files.\r\n    * **Customize:** Change the labels, IDs, and CSS class names in the starter HTML and CSS to match the fields in your schema (e.g., change `fieldA-1` to something specific like `status-1` or `priority-1`).\r\n\r\n2.  **Define Parallel Arrays (Data):** In your `script.js` file, find the \"Student Task 1\" section. Define three or more **parallel arrays** (lists) that hold the data for your custom app items.\r\n    * Each array must contain at least three examples.\r\n    * **Critical:** The item at the same **index** (e.g., index `[0]`) across all arrays must belong to the same single app item.\r\n    * *Example:* Define `const itemNames = [\"...\", \"...\", \"...\"];`\r\n\r\n3.  **Manually Wire the Data (JavaScript):** In the `script.js` file, first update the **DOM Element Hooks** variables (e.g., change `fieldA1` to your new variable name) to match your customized HTML IDs. Then, complete the empty `updateDisplay` function under \"Student Task 2\". Write code that uses **manual indexing** to assign array values to the correct HTML element.\r\n\r\n    * **Item 1:** Use the DOM variables for Item 1 (e.g., `title1`) and access the data at array **index `[0]`** (e.g., `itemNames[0]`).\r\n    * **Item 2:** Use the DOM variables for Item 2 (e.g., `title2`) and access the data at array **index `[1]`**.\r\n    * **Item 3:** Use the DOM variables for Item 3 (e.g., `title3`) and access the data at array **index `[2]`**.\r\n\r\n4.  **Test:** Run your code. The three items in your custom app's display should now correctly show the specific data you defined in your arrays.",
